  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Two pairs, one court – full-court 1v1",
  "description": "Full-court 1v1 is hard work and great practice, but with one pair at a time everyone else just watches. So run two pairs at once, going opposite ways. One pair starts on one baseline and attacks the far basket, the other starts on the opposite baseline. Set both pairs a little off centre, on different sides, so their paths only overlap a little around half-court.\n\nThe attacker dribbles up and the defender picks up at half-court; from there it is live to the basket and the rebound. To start the defence earlier, have the defender start closer and close out on the attacker at three-quarter court.\n\nThe next pair in line agree beforehand who attacks and who defends, and are ready to go. When the ball is dead, the pair gets off the court at once and runs to the line at the other end so the next pair can start. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Defence: low and wide, short quick steps, active hands – sprint to recover if the attacker gets past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Offence: eyes up, change pace and direction, and shield the ball with your body."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Be aware of the other pair as you pass each other near half-court."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Quick changeovers – the next pair should be on court as soon as the ball is dead."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
